WEBVTT

00:02:28.831 --> 00:02:31.331
Should you stick with A, or switch?

00:02:31.331 --> 00:02:33.011
Pause now to figure it out yourself

00:02:33.011 --> 00:02:33.771
Answer in 3

00:02:33.771 --> 00:02:36.170
Answer in 2

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.930
Answer in 1

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:40.600
For many Diskymon trainers,

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.772
it seems intuitive that if A 
is the best at beating B or C,

00:02:44.772 --> 00:02:48.772
it should also be the best at beating
B and C.

00:02:48.772 --> 00:02:53.052
Strangely enough, that couldn’t be
further from the truth.

00:02:53.052 --> 00:02:54.942
Let’s calculate the odds.

00:02:54.942 --> 00:02:58.942
For A to win, B has to summon
a level 2 Diskymon,

00:02:58.942 --> 00:03:01.962
and C has to summon a level 1.